[ti:ExecuTorch WebGPU: PyTorch Models in the Browser]
[ar:Ava & Brian]
[al:PyTorch Blog Podcast]
[00:00.00]Ava: A PyTorch model can now run on the GPU inside a browser tab, while prompts and outputs stay on the device.
[00:00.00]Ava：PyTorch 模型现在可以在浏览器标签页内的 GPU 上运行，提示词和输出都留在设备上。
[00:07.71]That's a useful path for private or offline inference.
[00:07.71]这为私密或离线推理提供了一条实用路径。
[00:11.99]Brian: ExecuTorch's new WebGPU backend makes that possible without converting the model to another framework's format.
[00:11.99]Brian：ExecuTorch 新增的 WebGPU 后端让这成为可能，无需把模型转换成其他框架的格式。
[00:21.26]You export it with torch.export to one .pte file, then run that file in a WebGPU browser.
[00:21.26]用 torch.export 导出一个 .pte 文件，再在支持 WebGPU 的浏览器中运行。
[00:29.04]Ava: The export path sounds simple. Where does the GPU work actually happen?
[00:29.04]Ava：导出流程听起来很简单。GPU 计算具体在哪里进行？
[00:34.94]Brian: The export uses WebGPUPartitioner.
[00:34.94]Brian：导出时会使用 WebGPUPartitioner。
[00:38.14]At runtime, ExecuTorch allocates GPU buffers and dispatches WGSL compute shaders through WebGPU command buffers.
[00:38.14]运行时，ExecuTorch 分配 GPU 缓冲区，并通过 WebGPU 命令缓冲区调度 WGSL 计算着色器。
[00:49.04]Ava: The same .pte file is meant to run across browsers and devices.
[00:49.04]Ava：同一个 .pte 文件可以在不同浏览器和设备上运行。
[00:53.94]What handles the differences?
[00:53.94]平台差异由谁处理？
[00:56.54]Brian: WGSL is translated to Metal Shading Language, SPIR-V, or HLSL, depending on the platform.
[00:56.54]Brian：WGSL 会根据平台转换为 Metal Shading Language、SPIR-V 或 HLSL。
[01:05.14]For the browser, the C++ runtime is compiled to WebAssembly with Emscripten, and emdawnwebgpu connects its WebGPU calls to the browser's JavaScript API.
[01:05.14]在浏览器中，C++ 运行时通过 Emscripten 编译成 WebAssembly，再由 emdawnwebgpu 将其 WebGPU 调用接入浏览器的 JavaScript API。
[01:20.17]Ava: A browser workload can change shape as a prompt grows.
[01:20.17]Ava：提示词变长时，浏览器中的计算形状也会变化。
[01:24.30]Does the backend reallocate GPU memory for every length?
[01:24.30]后端会为每种长度重新分配 GPU 内存吗？
[01:28.92]Brian: For dynamic shapes, it allocates buffers at the maximum size, recalculates workgroups for each dispatch, and routes shapes to specialized WGSL kernels.
[01:28.92]Brian：对于动态形状，它按最大尺寸分配缓冲区，每次调度时重新计算工作组，并根据形状选用专门的 WGSL 内核。
[01:40.65]That's how it supports batched prefill.
[01:40.65]这样就能支持批量预填充。
[01:44.03]Ava: That connects to the speed claim. What exactly was compared?
[01:44.03]Ava：这就说到速度提升了。具体比较了什么？
[01:48.89]Brian: The authors tested quantized Llama 3.2 1B and Qwen3-0.6B in Google Chrome on an Apple M1 Pro.
[01:48.89]Brian：作者在搭载 Apple M1 Pro 的设备上，用 Google Chrome 测试了量化版 Llama 3.2 1B 和 Qwen3-0.6B。
[01:57.68]They compared WebGPU with ExecuTorch's own multithreaded WebAssembly CPU backend using XNNPACK on the same machine.
[01:57.68]他们在同一台设备上，将 WebGPU 与 ExecuTorch 自带的、使用 XNNPACK 的多线程 WebAssembly CPU 后端作比较。
[02:08.90]Ava: And the reported gain is for prefill and decode, not one combined inference number, right?
[02:08.90]Ava：报告中的提速分别针对预填充和解码，不是合并后的单个推理指标，对吗？
[02:16.11]Brian: Right. WebGPU was 4–7× faster on prefill and 2–10× faster on decode in that setup.
[02:16.11]Brian：对。在这套测试环境下，WebGPU 的预填充速度快 4–7 倍，解码速度快 2–10 倍。
[02:23.54]Each point is the median of 5 runs after 3 warmups, across contexts from 128 to 8K tokens, with identical token IDs.
[02:23.54]上下文长度从 128 到 8K 个 token，使用相同的 token ID；每组数据先预热 3 次，再取 5 次运行的中位数。
[02:34.39]Ava: I'm looking at the precision settings before treating that as a pure GPU-versus-CPU result.
[02:34.39]Ava：在把它看作单纯的 GPU 与 CPU 对比前，我想先看看精度设置。
[02:40.89]Were the activation formats the same?
[02:40.89]激活值的格式一样吗？
[02:43.89]Brian: They weren't.
[02:43.89]Brian：不一样。
[02:45.03]WebGPU used 4-bit groupwise weights with group size 64 and fp32 activations.
[02:45.03]WebGPU 使用分组量化的 4 位权重，组大小为 64，激活值为 fp32。
[02:51.73]The CPU path used XNNPACK's 4-bit weights and 8-bit dynamic activations.
[02:51.73]CPU 路径使用 XNNPACK 的 4 位权重和 8 位动态量化激活值。
[02:58.07]Both paths were timed with wall-clock time because GPU timestamps aren't available for CPU execution.
[02:58.07]两条路径都用实际经过时间计时，因为 CPU 执行无法使用 GPU 时间戳。
[03:07.32]Ava: What does the model coverage look like beyond text generation?
[03:07.32]Ava：除了文本生成，还支持哪些模型？
[03:11.99]Brian: SmolVLM handles image questions and captions.
[03:11.99]Brian：SmolVLM 可处理图像问答和生成图片说明。
[03:15.51]The listed vision models cover depth estimation, image segmentation, object detection, super-resolution, and background removal.
[03:15.51]列出的视觉模型涵盖深度估计、图像分割、目标检测、超分辨率和背景移除。
[03:25.52]Whisper base covers speech-to-text, and another listed model covers text-to-speech.
[03:25.52]Whisper base 用于语音转文字，另一个列出的模型用于文字转语音。
[03:32.36]Ava: And the article includes on-device fine-tuning, not just inference.
[03:32.36]Ava：文章还介绍了设备端微调，不只是推理。
[03:37.80]Brian: Yes.
[03:37.80]Brian：是的。
[03:38.20]It lists LoRA and DiReFT fine-tuning for Llama 3.2 1B, Qwen2.5-0.5B, and Qwen3-0.6B, aimed at personalized assistants and domain adaptation.
[03:38.20]文中列出了 Llama 3.2 1B、Qwen2.5-0.5B 和 Qwen3-0.6B 的 LoRA 与 DiReFT 微调，用于个性化助手和领域适配。
[03:52.52]Ava: If I want to try it, what would I actually ship?
[03:52.52]Ava：如果我想试用，实际需要部署什么？
[03:56.28]Brian: The article describes serving a .pte file over a CDN on a web page.
[03:56.28]Brian：文章介绍了在网页上通过 CDN 提供 .pte 文件的方式。
[04:02.26]The ExecuTorch WebGPU Playground runs many of these models on the same WebAssembly + WebGPU runtime.
[04:02.26]ExecuTorch WebGPU Playground 使用同一套 WebAssembly + WebGPU 运行时运行其中许多模型。
[04:11.19]Each model's Hugging Face repository includes .pte files, a model card, and the exact export recipe.
[04:11.19]每个模型的 Hugging Face 仓库都包含 .pte 文件、模型卡片和完整的导出步骤。
[04:20.46]Ava: So the useful takeaway is one PyTorch export for local browser GPU inference, with a measured speedup over ExecuTorch's CPU path under the stated test conditions.
[04:20.46]Ava：所以关键是，一次 PyTorch 导出就能在浏览器里进行本地 GPU 推理；在所述测试条件下，相比 ExecuTorch 的 CPU 路径也有实测提速。
[04:33.10]Brian: And there's a broad set of validated models, plus on-device fine-tuning examples.
[04:33.10]Brian：此外，还有一批经过验证的模型，以及设备端微调示例。
[04:39.12]The backend's still in early development.
[04:39.12]这个后端仍处于早期开发阶段。
[04:42.17]The team plans to improve speed and stability and expand operator, data type, and model coverage.
[04:42.17]团队计划提升速度和稳定性，并扩大对算子、数据类型和模型的支持。
[04:49.37]Thanks for listening.
[04:49.37]感谢收听。
